<title>CHILE: Escondida reports higher copper output.</title>
<headline>Escondida reports higher copper output.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minera Escondida Limitada reported the following copper production figures for April.</p>
<p>COPPER (in metric tonnes)</p>
<p>     April 1997   March 1997   April 1996</p>
<p> Copper in concentrates	  72,139	 72,247	 69,269</p>
<p>Copper cathodes		    5,085	  4,671	  3,045</p>
<p>Total				 77,224	 76,918	 69,341</p>
<p>					Jan-April 1997   Jan-April 1996</p>
<p>Year-to-date			286,345	    244,981</p>
<p>					April 1997   March 1997   April 1996</p>
<p>GOLD (in ounces)		  14,126	 14,793	 14,344</p>
<p>The mine is owned by Broken Hill Proprietary and RTZ Corp plc.</p>
<p>((--Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
</text>
